Subject: [PATCH 2772/3799] soh: rename func_800353E8 ->
 Player_GetMeleeChargeLevel

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: returns Player.unk_834's neighbour unk_845, the field z_player_lib.c uses to stretch the spin attack; the field itself is unnamed
Defined in soh/src/code/z_actor.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_actor.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_actor.c b/soh/src/code/z_actor.c
index cf1795d8a..3c903e38e 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_actor.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_actor.c
@@ -4731,7 +4731,8 @@ s32 Actor_UpdateFallenItem(Actor* actor, PlayState* play) {
     return ret;
 }
 
-u8 func_800353E8(PlayState* play) {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_800353E8: returns Player.unk_834's neighbour unk_845, the field z_player_lib.c uses to stretch the spin attack; the field itself is unnamed
+u8 Player_GetMeleeChargeLevel(PlayState* play) {
     Player* player = GET_PLAYER(play);
 
     return player->unk_845;
